 verbatim, so a back-import is mandatory yet unenumerated."],"finding":"The reference inventory for moved names `_with_index_lock_retry` and `_backoff_sleep` omits gitutil's own RETAINED readers. `run_git_write` (gitutil.py:724, retained) calls `_with_index_lock_retry` (moved); `_with_transient_fault_retry` (gitutil.py:674, retained) calls `_backoff_sleep` (moved). The plan enumerates external importers and test consumers of these names but never records that gitutil must re-import them from git_locking so its retained bodies resolve — nor that category-(b) monkeypatch on `gitutil._backoff_sleep` stays load-bearing only if that back-import exists.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f003a4c9ed710b52a","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"\"Production importers the re-export must keep\" and \"Test consumers, by HOW they depend\" (b); dependency claim \"gitutil -> git_locking\"","norm_id":"n5722735d784cce03","priority":0.6611,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["gitutil.py:724 `run_git_write` raises NameError at runtime for `_with_index_lock_retry` if gitutil does not re-import the moved name from git_locking.","gitutil.py:674 `_with_transient_fault_retry` raises NameError for `_backoff_sleep` on the transient-retry path if not back-imported.","test_git_outcome.py:244/259 and test_gitutil_transient_write_retry.py:43 patch `gitutil._backoff_sleep`; unless gitutil retains a module-level `_backoff_sleep` the retained reader calls, the patch is silently vacuous (unslept backoff) or fails to bind — the exact category-(b) hazard the plan warns about, now applied to an intra-module reader it did not enumerate."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"In the re-export section, list `_with_index_lock_retry` and `_backoff_sleep` as names gitutil re-imports from git_locking specifically because its retained bodies (`run_git_write`, `_with_transient_fault_retry`) read them; then extend the category-(b) invocation probe to assert `gitutil._backoff_sleep` is the same object git_locking holds and that patching it changes the retained transient-retry path's behavior.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["1 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Resolve whether `_resolve_tracker_git_dir` belongs on the lock-contention seam: either keep it in `gitutil` alongside its docstring-siblings `_ticket_dirs`/`_dir_is_archived` (and let `git_locking` import it back), or move all three filesystem primitives and update the retained docstring so it no longer claims to own a moved function.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.6246,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan lists `_resolve_tracker_git_dir` under 'What moves'","gitutil.py:12-13: 'It also owns the tracker's shared FILESYSTEM primitives — ``_resolve_tracker_git_dir``, ``_ticket_dirs`` and ``_dir_is_archived``'","gitutil.py:72 `_resolve_tracker_git_dir` is a filesystem resolver (no git subprocess, no lock decision)","AC: 'The retained half of gitutil.py differs only in its docstring and import block' — the docstring still names a function the plan removes","Seam statement: 'git_locking.py DECIDES what happens when git's own locks are contended'"],"finding":"The plan moves `_resolve_tracker_git_dir` to `git_locking`, but that function is a pure filesystem git-dir resolver, not lock-contention decision logic, and the retained `gitutil` docstring (lines 12-18) explicitly classifies it as one of gitutil's owned 'shared FILESYSTEM primitives — _resolve_tracker_git_dir, _ticket_dirs and _dir_is_archived', co-located with two functions the plan keeps. Moving it contradicts the stated seam ('gitutil RUNS git; git_locking DECIDES lock contention') and leaves the retained docstring self-contradictory.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd7670db85fe826c7","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan 'What moves' vs 'The seam' / gitutil.py docstring lines 12-18","norm_id":"n2524b7ecc1f31da4","priority":0.0754,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Reviewer/maintainer reads the retained gitutil docstring and finds it references a function that no longer lives there","The seam boundary is muddied: a filesystem primitive ends up on the lock-decision side"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LL